---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import ServiceHeading from "../components/ServiceHeading.astro";
---
<Base title="Discuss a Part for Your Old Car — OCP3D" sheet="INTAKE · FIELD FILE">
  <section class="request-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <ServiceHeading
        eyebrow="OCP3D INTAKE · OPEN AN INVESTIGATION"
        title="Tell me what your old car needs."
        lede="Start with a missing part, a broken original, or a useful improvement the car never had. Send the car and problem—plus a number, photo, donor, or mounting detail if you have one—and I will reply to discuss the honest path forward."
        file="INTAKE · PARTS INVESTIGATION"
        signal="OBSERVE · TRACE · RESPOND"
      />

      <div class="case-content">
        <p class="dp1-line">This starts as an <b>OCP3D FIELD FILE</b>, then a human conversation—not
          an automatic quote or a promise that every part can be printed. The first job is to find
          the responsible next step.</p>
        <div class="tiers">
          <div class="tier"><span class="tier-n">01</span><b>You have the old part—even broken?</b> Best case for a restoration path. We can discuss measuring it, borrowing it, or using it as a donor for a documented replacement.</div>
          <div class="tier"><span class="tier-n">02</span><b>The car needs something it never had?</b> A cup holder, small storage solution, or other convenience idea starts with the actual console, trim, clearance, and what must not be blocked.</div>
          <div class="tier"><span class="tier-n">03</span><b>The part is gone or the route is unclear?</b> We can look for a donor, identify the interfaces that remain, or point you toward existing supply. Not every case starts with a print.</div>
        </div>

        <form id="case-form" class="case-file" method="post" action="/api/request">
          <div class="cf-head">
            <span class="cf-title">New case file</span>
            <span class="cf-no">OCP3D FIELD FILE · 3D</span>
          </div>
          <input type="hidden" name="type" value="request" />
          <input type="hidden" name="part_slug" value="" />
          <!-- honeypot: invisible to people, irresistible to bots -->
          <input type="text" name="company" class="hp" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" aria-hidden="true" />

          <div class="grid">
            <label>Your name
              <input type="text" name="name" required autocomplete="name" />
            </label>
            <label>Email
              <input type="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@garage.example" />
            </label>
            <label>The car
              <input type="text" name="vehicle" required placeholder="1984 Toyota Celica Supra" />
            </label>
            <label>The part or problem
              <input type="text" name="part" required placeholder="Sun visor clip, driver side — or a console cup holder" />
            </label>
            <label>OEM part № <span class="opt">if you have it</span>
              <input type="text" name="oem" placeholder="e.g. 58908-14010" />
            </label>
            <label>Where does the investigation start?
              <select name="situation">
                <option value="have-part">I have the old part (even broken)</option>
                <option value="on-car">It’s on the car, and it’s staying there</option>
                <option value="gone">The original part is gone entirely</option>
                <option value="improvement">It is a useful improvement the car never had</option>
                <option value="" selected>Not sure / it’s complicated</option>
              </select>
            </label>
          </div>
          <label class="full">Anything else
            <textarea name="message" rows="4" placeholder="What is missing, broken, inconvenient, or in the way? For an improvement, describe the mounting space and what must stay clear. Photos help — send them after you submit and we’ll match them to your case."></textarea>
          </label>

          <div class="cf-foot">
            <button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit">Open this investigation</button>
            <span class="cap">I will write back within a few days to discuss the part or improvement and the useful next step. Never spam.</span>
          </div>
          <p class="form-error" id="form-error" hidden></p>
        </form>

        <div class="done" id="case-done" hidden>
          <div class="done-stamp">Case opened</div>
          <p class="done-case">Case № <b id="case-id">—</b></p>
          <p>
            The conversation starts today. I’ll write from the workshop within a few days—replies
            to that email go straight to your case file, and photos are welcome.
          </p>
          <p class="done-alt">
            Nothing after a week? Email <a href="mailto:requests@lostclipsociety.com">requests@lostclipsociety.com</a>
            and reference your case number.
          </p>
        </div>

        <noscript>
          <p class="note">Submitting without JavaScript sends the same form — you’ll land on a
          confirmation page, or your mail app will open with everything pre-filled.</p>
        </noscript>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<script>
  const form = document.getElementById("case-form") as HTMLFormElement;
  const done = document.getElementById("case-done");
  const errBox = document.getElementById("form-error");

  // Registry empty states deep-link here with the human title and stable catalog slug.
  const params = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
  const partTitle = params.get("part");
  const partSlug = params.get("part_slug");
  if (partTitle) {
    const partInput = form.elements.namedItem("part") as HTMLInputElement;
    if (partInput && !partInput.value) partInput.value = partTitle;
  }
  if (partSlug && /^[a-z0-9-]+$/.test(partSlug)) {
    const slugInput = form.elements.namedItem("part_slug") as HTMLInputElement;
    if (slugInput) slugInput.value = partSlug;
  }

  form.addEventListener("submit", async (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    errBox.hidden = true;
    const btn = form.querySelector("button[type=submit]") as HTMLButtonElement;
    btn.disabled = true;
    btn.textContent = "Sending…";
    try {
      const res = await fetch(form.action, {
        method: "POST",
        body: new FormData(form),
        headers: { accept: "application/json" },
      });
      const data = await res.json();
      if (res.ok && data.ok) {
        document.getElementById("case-id").textContent = data.case;
        form.hidden = true;
        done.hidden = false;
        done.scrollIntoView({ behavior: "smooth", block: "center" });
      } else if (data.unconfigured) {
        // Backend not wired yet — fall back to a prefilled email.
        const f = new FormData(form);
        const subject = `OCP3D investigation — ${f.get("part")} (${f.get("vehicle")})`;
        const body = [
          `Name: ${f.get("name")}`, `Email: ${f.get("email")}`, `Vehicle: ${f.get("vehicle")}`,
          `Part or problem: ${f.get("part")}`, `OEM №: ${f.get("oem") || "—"}`
          `Situation: ${(f.get("situation") as string) || "—"}`, "", (f.get("message") as string) || "",
        ].join("\n");
        window.location.href = `mailto:requests@lostclipsociety.com?subject=${encodeURIComponent(subject)}&body=${encodeURIComponent(body)}`;
      } else {
        throw new Error(data.error ?? "failed");
      }
    } catch (err) {
      errBox.textContent = "That did not transmit. Check the required fields and try again — or email requests@lostclipsociety.com directly.";
      errBox.hidden = false;
      btn.disabled = false;
      btn.textContent = "Open this investigation";
    }
  });
</script>

<style>
  .request-page { background: linear-gradient(180deg, color-mix(in srgb, var(--ground-deep) 28%, transparent), transparent 35%); }
  .request-page .wrap { display: grid; gap: 18px; }
  .case-content { width: min(100%, 900px); margin-inline: auto; }
  .dp1-line { color: var(--steel); font-size: var(--t-dense); letter-spacing: .04em; max-width: 70ch; }
  .dp1-line b { color: var(--signal); }
  .tiers { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 14px; margin: 20px 0 24px; }
  .tier {
    position: relative; min-height: 166px; background: var(--ground-deep); border: var(--bd-inner) solid var(--rule);
    padding: 43px 18px 18px; font-size: var(--t-dense); color: var(--steel); line-height: var(--t-section-lh);
  }
  .tier-n { position: absolute; top: 14px; left: 18px; font-size: var(--t-micro); letter-spacing: var(--t-micro-tr); color: var(--ion); }
  .tier b { color: var(--paper); display: block; margin-bottom: 7px; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--h-step); text-transform: uppercase; }

  .case-file { background: var(--panel); color: var(--paper); border: var(--bd-inner) solid var(--rule-2); padding: 30px; }
  .cf-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 14px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--signal); padding-bottom: 11px; margin-bottom: 22px; }
  .cf-title { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 20px; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .cf-no { font-size: var(--t-eyebrow); color: var(--signal); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: var(--t-eyebrow-tr); }
  .hp { position: absolute; left: -9999px; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; }
  .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 15px 20px; }
  label { display: grid; gap: 7px; font-size: var(--t-eyebrow); letter-spacing: var(--t-eyebrow-tr); text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--steel); }
  label .opt { text-transform: none; letter-spacing: .02em; opacity: .75; }
  input, select, textarea { font: inherit; font-size: .85rem; padding: 12px; background: var(--ground-deep); border: var(--bd-inner) solid var(--rule); color: var(--paper); letter-spacing: normal; text-transform: none; width: 100%; }
  input:focus, select:focus, textarea:focus { outline: 2px solid var(--ion); outline-offset: 1px; }
  .full { margin-top: 20px; }
  textarea { resize: vertical; }
  .cf-foot { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; margin-top: 20px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .cap { font-size: var(--t-eyebrow); color: var(--steel); max-width: 40ch; }
  .form-error { color: var(--signal); font-size: var(--t-dense); margin: 14px 0 0; }

  .done { background: var(--panel); color: var(--paper); border: var(--bd-inner) solid var(--rule-2); padding: 30px; }
  .done-stamp { display: inline-block; font-size: var(--t-dense); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: var(--t-eyebrow-tr); text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--signal); border: 1px solid var(--signal); padding: 6px 10px; transform: rotate(-2deg); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .done-case { font-size: .95rem; color: var(--paper); }
  .done p { color: var(--steel); }
  .done-alt { font-size: var(--t-eyebrow); }
  .done-alt a, .note a { color: var(--ion); }

  @media (max-width: 760px) { .tiers { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .tier { min-height: auto; } }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .case-file { padding: 20px; } .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .cf-head { align-items: flex-start; flex-direction: column; } }
</style>
